  "cause": {
    "proximate_text": "The direct cause of the condition was that the pilot valve for the Reactor Feed Pump \"B\" Minimum Flow Valve's positioner stuck in a position that resulted in the minimum flow valve going closed. This directly resulted in the RFP low suction flow condition that tripped RFP B. The root cause of the event was that the Reactor Feed Pump \"B\" Minimum Flow Valve positioner installed during Preventive Maintenance activities failed due to infant mortality within approximately 29 hours of service ... a latent issue (manufacturer defect) not identified by functional testing at the time the part was received.",
    "cause_code": "TBD",
    "category": "provisional",
    "theme": "positioner infant-mortality / latent manufacturer defect not caught by receipt testing",
    "provisional": true
  },
